From 05bdf13d7cec19ae7576594bad981c155457ebba Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: woahwhattheheck <woahwhattheheck@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 12:09:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 03/10] Cast: Add CastV2 channel to talk to receivers directly

CastChannel speaks the Cast v2 control protocol on the receiver's TLS
port: length-prefixed CastMessage frames (proto schema added, generated
with Wire), the deviceauth challenge, virtual connections to receiver-0
and to launched applications, and the heartbeat (PING every 5 s,
answering the receiver's PINGs, closing after 20 s without traffic).

CastDeviceSession builds the receiver namespace on top of it:
GET_STATUS, LAUNCH (joining a running instance unless relaunch is
requested), STOP, SET_VOLUME, joining by application id and/or session
id, and leaving an application without stopping it. Receiver requests
use their own request ids and only replies from receiver-0 on the
receiver namespace are matched against them, so ids chosen by client
applications for their own namespaces can not collide. Everything runs
on one session thread so callbacks keep their order and no binder
thread blocks on the network.
